The `await` was removed from the user mutation:

::diff{file="packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/featureOptIn/_router.ts" lines="103-110"}

The mutation now returns `{ success: true }` right away, before the write finishes. Any failure becomes an unhandled promise rejection instead of a tRPC error. That includes the new scope-validation `ErrorWithCode(BadRequest)` this PR adds and the Prisma error from the swapped-branch bug. So the client thinks the change was saved when it wasn't, and the scope check is effectively invisible to callers.

The team and org mutations below still `await` correctly.

